cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and the
  accompanying paper (see `preferred-citation`).
title: >-
  lifted-mpcc-dd: a domain-decomposition IPOPT linear solver for the lifted
  TV-denoising MPCC
abstract: >-
  Companion code for the domain-decomposition (arrowhead / Schur-complement)
  linear solver used inside IPOPT to solve the bilevel total-variation image
  denoising problem written as a lifted mathematical program with complementarity
  constraints (MPCC), in the unit-ball dual formulation. The C++ plugin injects a
  custom SparseSymLinearSolverInterface that produces every interior-point Newton
  step by domain decomposition (local HSL MA57/MA97 factorizations plus a direct
  or preconditioned-CG interface solve), answering IPOPT's inertia query via the
  Haynsworth identity without ever factorizing the full KKT. Ships with Python
  helpers that generate byte-identical solver inputs from the extracted reference
  formulation and render the result figures.
